SUMMARY:CANCELLED - Teen Book Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T190000
UID:cb8b7f7a23cf7a010286cd386dd4a4b8@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Teens\n\nFor Teens ages 13-18 years of age only.Ca
 lling all teen readers! Join us for Teen Book Talk\, a fun and engaging mo
 nthly book discussion group led by members of our Teen Advisory Board! Boo
 k selections are chosen by teens during advisory meetings. Interested in j
 oining the Teen Advisory Board? Sign up through the library calendar. Each
  month\, we’ll dive into a new title—ranging from trending young adult
  fiction to graphic novels\, fantasy epics\, thought-provoking contemporar
 y stories\, and more.You’ll get the chance to share your thoughts\, hear
  different perspectives\, and connect with fellow book lovers in a relaxed
  and welcoming space. Snacks will be provided\, and occasionally we’ll h
 ave themed activities or giveaways tied to the book!Note: To help everyone
  stay present and get the most out of the experience\, we ask that all pho
 nes stay in pockets or bags during the program. Thank you for your coopera
 tion!Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their r
 egistration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted
  from registering for future programs for a period of one month’s time. 
 Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of th
 e program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their c
 hange in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes pr
 ior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstanc
 es. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\,
  your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted
  entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. How
 ever\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes pa
 st the start time.Check In - All participants must provide an emergency co
 ntact number upon registration or at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-book-talk-156961
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
