BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Storm Science: The Real Meteorology Behind the Movies
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T200000
UID:0252bfee45458de96b22420973fb46f5@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Presentation\, STEM\, Virtual\, Adults\, Seniors\n
 \nAre you fascinated by the sheer power of extreme weather? ⚡ Ever wonde
 red how much of Hollywood’s natural disaster movies is actually based on
  real science? 🎬Join us at the library for a special virtual presentati
 on with Kyle Elliott\, Director of the Weather Information Center at Mille
 rsville University\, for an inside look at the wild world of meteorology! 
 Kyle will be joining us live via Zoom on our big screen to dive deep into 
 the science of our atmosphere.Designed specifically for adults who love to
  know how things work\, this program will cover:🚗 Storm Chasing & Field
  Research: What it’s actually like to pursue severe thunderstorms and to
 rnadoes in the field to study extreme conditions.🔮 Weather Forecasting:
  How meteorologists predict major weather events before they hit.❄️ Lo
 cal Winter Storms: A look into the powerful winter weather systems that sh
 ape our local climate.🚨 Weather Safety: Understanding the critical diff
 erences between weather watches and warnings to keep you weather-ready.Bri
 ng your curiosity for a live Q&A session with Kyle following the presentat
 ion! 🗣️❓🎟️ Registration is recommended to ensure your seat in 
 the room. Sign up today!
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-adult-services-
 program-183002
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
