BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Q & A and Signing featuring Lauren Willig in conversation w
 ith Lindsay Hameroff
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T203000
UID:979b1e24391c7b524ce9b9e9c12a1f96@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Fundraiser\, Everyone\n\nGet your tickets HERE!Joi
 n the Columbia Public Library and Book Bar for a night to remember! Author
  Lauren Willig will be in conversation with author Lindsay Hameroff about 
 Willig's newest title\, What Happens at Nightfall. Ticket required\; all t
 ickets include a hardcover copy of What Happens at Nightfall by Lauren Wil
 lig (fulfilled by local indie bookstore Book Bar with 50% of profits going
  to the Columbia Public Library). Lindsay Hameroff's latest title\, Rewrit
 e the Stars\, will also be available for purchase separately at the event.
  Both authors will be available to sign copies of their books after the Q&
 A portion.Schedule:5:30pm: Doors open6:30pm-7:30pm: Author conversation wi
 th Lauren Willig and Lindsay Hameroff\, including time for audience Q&A7:3
 0pm-8:30pm: Author signingParking: Free on-street parking at the library a
 nd the school lot next door. Church lot reserved for event staff only. Eve
 nt is located at St. John's Evangelical Lutheran Church in their Fellowshi
 p Hall (616 Locust Street\, Columbia\, PA). Attendees may enter on the 6th
  Street Side (directly across from the library) at the RED doors. ADA acce
 ss is available upon request. For ADA access requests\, please reach out i
 n advance to Heather Beury at hbeury@columbiapubliclibrary.org for accommo
 dation.About the Authors:Lauren Willig is the New York Times and USA Today
  bestselling author of more than twenty-five works of fiction\, including 
 The Girl from Greenwich Street\, Band of Sisters\, the RITA Award-winning 
 Pink Carnation series\, and five novels co-written with Beatriz Williams a
 nd Karen White. Her books have been translated into over twenty languages\
 , picked for Book of the Month Club\, awarded the RITA\, Booksellers Best\
 , and Golden Leaf awards\, and chosen for the American Library Association
 ’s annual list of the best genre fiction. An alumna of Yale University\,
  she has a graduate degree in history from Harvard and a JD from Harvard L
 aw School. She lives in New York City with her husband\, two young childre
 n\, and vast quantities of coffee.Lindsay Hameroff is a bestselling writer
 \, humorist\, and former English teacher raised in Baltimore\, Maryland\, 
 and based in Harrisburg\, Pennsylvania. Her writing has been featured in M
 cSweeney’s Internet Tendency\, Weekly Humorist\, and fan letters to Harr
 y Styles. She is the author of Till There Was You\, her debut novel\, Neve
 r Planned on You\, and Rewrite the Stars.Event Location: St. John's Evange
 lical Lutheran Church\, Columbia\, PA. (616 Locust Street). Please see par
 king information in event description.
LOCATION:Columbia
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/author-q-and-signing-fea
 turing-lauren-willig-conversation-lindsay-hameroff-200276
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
