 edge and observation skills into action through hands-on explorations you 
 will unmask the clues that today’s scientists use to solve crimes. You w
 ill be guided through important aspects of scientific investigations using
  the same forensic clues that detectives rely upon in their work. Looking 
 at several aspects of forensic science\, “crime scenes” will be invest
 igated by studying finger prints\, visual clues and observations and bones
 . The vital role of insects in the wild will also be examined as it pertai
 ns to forensic science.Ages 10 - 15.Limit 30 youth. Registration required.
  Youth may attend without a caregiver\; however\, we do ask that the careg
 iver remains present in the building during the program. THANK YOU\, Colum
 bia Fraternal Association for sponsoring this program.
